    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d42">

                <pb facs="0177" n="92" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg92"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.60f11/17: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Czechoslovakia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Crane</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Prague</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-10-22T17:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 22,
                                1919, 5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received 5.15
                            p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>42. Mr. John Masaryk, son of President Masaryk, sails on auxiliary <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Baltic</hi> October 29 for Washington to be first
                    Secretary of Czecho-Slovak Legation and Chargé d’Affaires pending the arrival of
                    Doctor Stepanek, [see] my number 15 September 26 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >27</hi>],<anchor n="7" xml:id="d42-f1"/> who will not be able leave Prague
                    for several months. Request customary courtesies be extended Masaryk.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
